{#
  A confirmed `maps` entry: a plain link to the business's Google Maps place page.

  Same shape and same accessibility guarantees as entry-link.njk - a real <a href>, one box,
  the 44x44 CSS px floor from base.css (FR-023). It is a separate partial only because the
  destination is derived from `placeId` rather than read from a `url` key.

  It is a LINK and nothing more. No web API can add a place to a customer's Google saved
  list, so the hub does not pretend to offer one; the customer saves it themselves from the
  page this opens.
#}
<li class="entries__item">
  <a class="entry entry--link entry--maps" href="{{ resolve.resolveHref(entry, business) }}" rel="noopener">
    <span class="entry__label">{{ entry.label }}</span>
  </a>
</li>
